Z||000000||Stungbymystang||11-25-2001||04:27 AM||||Hey guys, I just wanted to let yall know the Fiero has been one of my favorite cars for a long time now. I have never owned one or even so much as ridden in one. I have heard all kinds of things but one I think may be true, is that the last 2 years Pontiac made the Fiero it was awesome, but before that is really kind of sucked. I hate it too, because I feel like Pontiac tried a little to late when it came to that car.<P>On a side note I do drive a mustang, but I have no idea why I love those little cars so damn much. My question is this.<BR>Who has the fastest Fiero here? ¼ mile times, etc. I know nothing about them mechanically so please pardon my ignorance. I just found this board tonight and just thought it would be cool to meet some Fiero enthusiast and ask some questions!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Check Her Out <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/xvwannabemevx/home.html" TARGET=_blank>Jade Not Your Average 6</A><BR>94, v6 Auto. 144,220 miles (engine rebuilt @ 139,330)<P>Mods:<BR>K&N, Duals w/flowmasters, Mac 1 5/8 headers<BR>Crank Underdrive Pulley<BR>3.73's<BR>JMS Chip <P>Sounds: <BR>Alpine Head Unit<BR>3 Alpine V12's, 1 JL Audio 500/1<BR>2 JL 12's, 2 Kenwood 6x9's, 2 Kenwood 5x7's, 6 Alpine Tweets||||reg||1
Z||000001||donny||11-25-2001||04:36 AM||||Welcome to the board.I believe the person with the fastest car on the forum runs a 10 second quarter mile.(don't remember who's car it is though)I'm sure someone will answer that question.We do have quite a few people on here who consistently run low 12's.Glad to see another fiero enthusiast.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Stungbymystang||11-25-2001||04:42 AM||||That is cool as hell. I have never seen anyone with a modified Fiero so it is cool to know yall are out there. I wish I had some spare cash to pick one up. Just looking around on this board makes me want to go out and buy one!!!! But if I got it, I would have to modify it and I can’t really have 2 projects going on at once. If I were to pick up a used one, would there be any major concerns for me to look for? Was I correct about the later years being the best? I know personally I like the looks better, but I really like them all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||11-25-2001||05:08 AM||||Welcome to the forum! If you want a used fiero I suggest you take a trip to Toney AL. It's just a little north of Huntsville. Ed Parks owns the Fiero Factory. I went there once but no one was their. He does engine swaps and full restos. Oops, I'm starting to babble. Only two more hours of this twelve hour work day left...<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">   <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Kelvin Vivian||11-25-2001||06:21 AM||||Went by the GoodYear shop to pick up a couple of tires and a couple of people at the shop asked me questions about my Fiero...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It's nice to hear from those whi appreciate these two-seaters...<P>Here's a quick breakdown of the Fiero by years:<P>1984 <BR>base coupe - 4-spd (econo tranny), 4-cyl<BR>sport coupe - 4-spd (econo or performance) or auto (3-spd), 4-cyl<BR>SE - same as sport coupe<BR>Indy Fiero - 4-spd (performance) with 4-cyl<P>1985 (minor suspension tweaks made this year, radius of turning circle decreased)<BR>base coupe - 5-spd, 4-cyl<BR>sport coupe - 5-spd or auto, 4-cyl<BR>SE - 5-spd or auto with 4-cyl, 4-spd or auto with V6<BR>GT - 4-spd or auto with V6<P>1986 (this year, the GTs were redesigned with a "Fastback" rear, more minor suspension tweaks)<BR>same as 1985, except some late model 86 SEs and GTs with V6s had "upgraded" 5-spd trannys to replace the 4-spds.<P>1987 (front headlight motors "upgraded", gas tank enlarged from 10.2gal to 11.9, all V6 Fieros have a 5-spd tranny, minor suspension tweaks made)<BR>coupe - 5-spd or auto, 4-cyl<BR>SE - 5-spd or auto, 4-cyl or V6<BR>GT - 5-spd or auto with V6<P>1988 (suspension redesign occured for this model year)<BR>coupe - 5-spd or auto with 4-cyl<BR>Formula - 5-spd or auto with V6<BR>GT - same as Formula<P>KV<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=3&courtesy=1">    <BR>88 GT, 5-spd<BR>87 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd||||reg||14
Z||000005||Old Lar||11-25-2001||10:03 AM||||The fastest Fiero is hard to quantify.  Fastest duke, stock 2.8, fastest 3.1, 3.4, 3.8.  Or Fastest V8.  Fastest as in eigth mile, quarter mile or fastest as in top speed.<P>At the FOCOA convention in Williamsbug an 88 coupe dragster with a 455 Pontiac engine had time slips of 98 mph for the 1/8 mile.<P>So what ever niche you want, there will be a "fastest Fiero" in it.||||reg||1
